  "id": "COMPOUND:23876 - PROTEIN:935",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 3-O-Methyl-beta-D-glucopyranose and Dihydropteroate synthase 1, mediated through Alpha-2 adrenergic receptors. This pathway is supported by two distinct but overlapping connections: one through Tussilagine and another through valsartan. Both Tussilagine and valsartan are known to interact with Alpha-2 adrenergic receptors, which in turn target Dihydropteroate synthase 1. The shared involvement of Alpha-2 adrenergic receptors as a common intermediate in both pathways strengthens the hypothesis that 3-O-Methyl-beta-D-glucopyranose may influence Dihydropteroate synthase 1 via this receptor-mediated mechanism. The evidence is consistent across two different compounds, suggesting a possible pharmacological role of 3-O-Methyl-beta-D-glucopyranose in modulating the activity of Dihydropteroate synthase 1 through the Alpha-2 adrenergic receptor pathway.",
